# Scripted edits stay byte-clean across the mac/windows pair (MIGRATION.md
# section 4 -- the WINVM lesson: a CRLF slip corrupts golden transcripts and
# .mst world sources that both repos share verbatim).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one deliberate exception: Strongtalk's original reference pages carry
# CRLF in the blobs themselves, inherited from MACVM and from the 2002 release
# before it. They are a historical archive — served as static assets, never
# parsed by the VM, and `gui/` is not even in the Windows workspace.
# Normalizing them would be a ~9,300-line diff that diverges 64 files from
# MACVM upstream and buys nothing. Marked here so the state is intentional
# rather than an anomaly the next sweep "corrects".
gui/reference/** -text
